bring class/algebra/total/hath_add.tung
bring type/two.tung

## flipping, and `b -+ a`, which flippeth `b` and addeth `a`: `a` less `b`.
## each type supplieth `-+` directly, so integers and floats subtract in one
## native step; `group_+` and `ring` prove that it agreeth with flipping and
## `+`.
show class hath_-: [α: *, *] {
  let -: [α, α]

  let -+: [α, α, α]
}

## `+` on `𝟚` is exclusive or, so each value is its own flipping.
bizen: 𝟚 hath_- {
  let -: [a:] ≔ a

  let -+: [a:, b:] ≔ a + b
}
